   "title": "Model files",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Files on this box:\n- diffusion_models/krea2_turbo_int8_convrot (int8 build of Krea 2 Turbo)\n- text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled (CLIPLoader type: krea2)\n- vae/qwen_image_vae\n- loras/krea2_identity_edit_v1_2 (conradlocke/krea2-identity-edit) @ 1.0, first\n- loras/RealisticSnapshotKrea2 (CivitAI 2268008 / 3084537) @ 1.0 to 1.5, stacked after it\n\nSettings from the guide: 8 to 12 steps (10), cfg 1, euler, ref_boost 2 to 6 (4 = strong face lock), grounding_px 768 to 1024 (1024 for faces), fit_mode fit, output <= 2 MP.\nIf the face drifts when Realistic Snapshot is raised: lower it or raise ref_boost.\n\nTwo-image try-on: image 1 = person, image 2 = garment product photo (enable group 2)."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 101,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    640,
    330
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    190
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 7,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How inputs work",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "PERSON reference (group 1): one clear photo of your model.\n- Upright (a tilted selfie kills the likeness), face well lit,\n  about 1 MP. Crop to head-and-shoulders or half body.\n- Whatever is in this photo tends to come along: hats, flower\n  crowns, glasses, people behind. Say 'remove the flower crown'\n  or 'plain background' in the prompt if you do not want them.\n- The same reference photo can be reused for every product."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 102,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    640,
    1130
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    210
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 8,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Enable for two-image edits",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "GARMENT / TRY-ON (group 2, bypassed by default).\nEnable: right-click the group title -> toggle Bypass off.\n\nImage 2 = the product photo (flat-lay or on a hanger, plain\nbackground works best, about 1 MP).\nPrompt: 'Put the garment from the second image on the person,\nkeeping all other aspects of the image the same.'\nAdd pose / scene changes after that sentence if wanted.\n\nOrder rule: person = image 1 (group 1), garment = image 2 (here)."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 103,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1620,
    360
   ],
   "size": [
    620,
    300
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 9,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Writing instructions",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Prompt patterns that worked (short, plain English):\n\nOutfit:  'Change her outfit to a black turtleneck and grey wool\n          trousers. Keep the same face and hair.'\nAngle:   'Change the camera angle to a side profile view, full\n          body, walking on a city sidewalk. Keep the same face,\n          hair and outfit.'\nScene:   'Change the scene to a bright minimalist clothing store,\n          standing, looking at the camera.'\nTry-on:  'Put the garment from the second image on the person,\n          keeping all other aspects of the image the same.'\n\nAlways end with 'Keep the same face and hair.' unless you are\nchanging the hair. Long instruction lists work worse than 2 to 3\nshort sentences. grounding_px 768 = trained range; go 1024 if the\nface comes out generic, 512 if the edit is ignored."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 104,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    2320,
    230
   ],
   "size": [
    420,
    420
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 10,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Fidelity dial",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "ref_boost (person in prompt-only mode, garment in try-on mode)\nand ref_boost_a (person in try-on mode): 4 = recommended.\nRaise to 6 if the face drifts; above ~8 the outfit / pose edit\nstarts being ignored (over-copy).\n\nRealistic Snapshot LoRA: 1.0 default. Raise toward 1.5 for a\nstronger phone-photo / skin-texture look; lower it (or bypass\nthe brown node) if the likeness suffers.\n\nfit_mode: fit (default). Output <= 2 MP; 1 MP is the sweet spot."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 105,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    2800,
    490
   ],
   "size": [
    320,
    280
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 11,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Sampling",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Krea 2 Turbo: 10 steps, cfg 1, euler / simple.\n  8 steps  = follows the instruction more\n  12 steps = more detail / likeness\nSeed: randomize. Batch a few seeds per product and pick the best.\nWhen an edit is ignored (e.g. removing an accessory), try the\nRaw model at cfg 3 / 20 steps, per the node README."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 106,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
